Confirmed from the code, not inferred — `dispatch.mjs:111`, the **exactly-once-per-slot** rule:

```js
if (family.some((i) => (i.title ?? '').trim() === title)) {
  return { action: 'skip', reason: `dispatch issue for slot ${slotId} already exists (exactly-once)` };
}
```

The title match ignores state. Issues #66/#68 were filed for slot `d2026-08-06` by the *failing* runs, so that slot's one dispatch is spent — closing them can't give it back. The agent stage will run on the **`d2026-08-07` slot**, tomorrow, unattended.

That's a real finding, so I'm recording it where it belongs:

